Scope: the src/ delta b5c0b95..356321e is the delta of the previous record
b5c0b95-1f274a2 (canonical e7f7ed8 is code-identical to 1f274a2) plus two
landings. Snag regularised-hors-bcdcdd84 (67bafc1, de17547, 408b5a7;
canonical fdd4587) touches adaptive_warmup_mcmc.jl,
completion_warmup_mcmc.jl, kwarg_validation.jl and Reparametrizations.jl.
Snag built-an-indexed-3fed939c (f920651; canonical 356321e) touches
Reparametrizations.jl only. That second landing added no record of its own,
so this one record covers both hops to the live tip. With
`divergence_tolerance` at its default, `_halve_stepsize!` returns before
any effect. The only other per-transition work added is a sum of the
acceptance statistic over retained draws, which consumes no randomness. At
a restart the dual-averaging object is rebuilt only when the recorded
target differs from the current one, which needs a halving. The shared
`_drop_retained_draws!` empties the retained draws a few statements
earlier than before, before the reparametrization and transformation
reselection, which read only the halo. `maybecall` now treats a `Number`
as a constant and calls everything else, where before it called a
`Function` and treated everything else as a constant. The two rules agree
on closures and numbers, the only accessor arguments any harness passes.
f920651 adds `_is_accessor` / `_check_accessors`, which the
`IndexedReparametrization` constructor runs once on its first pair: they
throw for an argument that is neither `Real` nor callable and otherwise
return `nothing`, and its other edits are docstrings and error text. A
harness whose accessors failed that check (the BRM harnesses build theirs
inside BRM) would stop with an error, not produce different numbers.
The benchmark driver and docs/benchmark/Project.toml are byte-identical
across the two measured revisions; common.jl differs only in comments and
the dirty-source check's inclusion of ext/.

Limits: one seed and the four funnel arms provide output-identity
evidence, not a timing or performance claim. This does not re-measure
posteriordb, BRM, linear-restart, nonlinear-weighting or gradient-overhead
artifacts. Their continued applicability rests on the source-path
reasoning above. The four SCOPEd gradient probes, measured at fbe9030 and
b35a718, are code-identical to b5c0b95 within their scope
(src/Reparametrizations.jl, src/WarmupHMC.jl, ext/), and the scoped
changes since are the `maybecall` dispatch and the construction-time
check above. Runs that opt into
`divergence_tolerance` have deliberately new behaviour and are outside
